$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7-(1,3-Dimethyl-5-(phenoxymethyl)-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-1-(2-morpholinoethyl)-3-(3-(naphthalen-1-yloxy)propyl)-1H-indole-2-carboxylic
Acid (22). A suspension of compound 21 (1.14 g, 3.62 mmol), phenol (0.338
g, 3.59 mmol), cesium carbonate (1.24 g, 3.80 mmol), and DMF (5 mL) was
stirred at ambient temperature overnight. The reaction was partitioned
between EtOAc and water. The organic layer was washed 2× with brine,
dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated to provide 0.535 g (54%) of
crude material which was carried forward as such. A suspension of the
above intermediate (0.535 g, 1.63 mmol), compound 15 (0.826 g, 1.65
mmol), Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (0.116 g, 0.16 mmol), K2CO3 (0.342. g, 1.48 mmol) in
DMF (66 mL) and water (8 mL) was heated to 100 °C for 4 h. The reaction
mixture was concentrated. The residue was partitioned between EtOAc and
water. The aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic
layers were washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated to
crude product. The crude product was loaded onto a plug of silica gel and
eluted (50-100% EtOAc/hexanes) to provide 0.741 g (78%) of a yellow
solid. A suspension of the above intermediate (0.741 g, 1.29 mmol),
tetrabutylammonium bromide (0.092 g, 0.284 mmol), cesium carbonate (1.26
g, 3.87 mmol), and 4-(2-chloroethyl)morpholine (0.264 g, 1.42 mmol) in
DMF (10 mL) was heated to 80 °C for 18 h. The reaction mixture was
partitioned between water and dichloromethane. The organic layer was
washed with water and brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated. The residue was purified by flash chromatography (3%
MeOH/EtOAc) to provide 0.631 g (71%) of a yellow solid. To the above
intermediate (0.631 g, 0.919 mmol) dissolved in THF (20 mL) and water (8
mL) was added LiOH (2 M, 1 mL). The reaction was heated to 50 °C for 16
h. The reaction mixture was quenched with 1 N HCl (2 mL) to adjust to pH
7. The mixture was extracted with dichloromethane, dried over Na2SO4,
filtered, and concentrated. The residue was purified by reverse phase
preparative HPLC (C-18, 40-100% MeCN/H2O/0.1% TFA). 0.133 mg (22%) of the
title compound. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.243-8.267 (m, 1H),
7.792-7.824 (m, 2H), 7.440-7.482 (m, 2H), 7.401 (d, J = 8 Hz, 1H), 7.313
(t, J = 8 Hz, 1H), 7.157 (t, J = 8 Hz, 2H), 7.082-7.096 (m, 2H), 6.864
(t, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H), 6.707-6.764 (m, 3H), 4.977 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H),
4.780-4.830 (m, 1H), 4.519-4.593 (m, 1H), 4.180 (t, J = 5.4 Hz, 2H),
3.946 (s, 3H), 3.869 (br, 4H), 3.812 (s, 2H), 3.472-3.518 (m, 2H),
3.135-3.204 (m, 2H), 2.993-3.083 (m, 2H), 2.315-2.381 (m, 2H), 2.196 (s,
3H). LC-MS (ESI): m/z 659.0 (M + H+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction (stage 2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
